From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:46:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: skip the VLAN notification when the ubus context is gone

The VLAN teardown of a BSS runs after the ubus object of that BSS is
gone. If the BSS held the last reference, hostapd freed the shared
ubus context by then. The VLAN removal notification then dereferences
a null context, and hostapd crashes during a disable or during the
restart of a DFS fallback.

Skip the notification when no ubus context exists.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/ap/ubus.c |    5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ap/ubus.c
+++ b/src/ap/ubus.c
@@ -3186,6 +3186,11 @@ hostapd_ubus_vlan_action(struct hostapd_
 	void *c;
 	int i;
 
+	/* vlan_deinit() runs after hostapd_ubus_free_bss() may have dropped the
+	 * last reference and freed the shared context */
+	if (!ctx)
+		return;
+
 	if (!obj->has_subscribers)
 		return;
 
